From: arch-port
Subject: [PATCH] cpu, gpu_fdinfo: MediaTek thermal zone names

MediaTek's LVTS thermal driver names its hwmon devices after the zones:
cpu_big0_thermal .. cpu_big3_thermal, cpu_little0_thermal .., gpu0_thermal,
gpu1_thermal. The CPU match (cpu\d*_thermal) and the panfrost GPU lookup
("gpu_thermal") found neither, so no temperatures were shown.
---
--- a/src/cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/cpu.cpp
@@ -609,7 +609,8 @@
             // E2K (Elbrus 2000) CPU temperature module
             find_input(path, "temp", input, "Node 0 Max");
             break;
-        } else if (std::regex_match(name, match, std::regex("cpu\\d*_thermal"))) {
+        } else if (std::regex_match(name, match, std::regex("cpu(_big)?\\d*_thermal"))) {
+            // cpu_big<N>_thermal: MediaTek LVTS zones (the big cores run hottest)
             find_fallback_input(path, "temp1", input);
             break;
         } else if (name == "apm_xgene") {
--- a/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
+++ b/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
@@ -177,8 +177,12 @@
 
     if (module == "msm")
         hwmon = find_hwmon_sensor_dir("gpu");
-    else if (module == "panfrost" || module == "panthor")
+    else if (module == "panfrost" || module == "panthor") {
         hwmon = find_hwmon_sensor_dir("gpu_thermal");
+        // MediaTek LVTS names its GPU zones gpu0_thermal, gpu1_thermal
+        if (hwmon.empty())
+            hwmon = find_hwmon_sensor_dir("gpu0_thermal");
+    }
     else
         hwmon = find_hwmon_dir();
 
